Package: BregSurv
Type: Package
Title: Transfer Learning for Time-to-Event Models via a Unified Bregman-Divergence Objective
Version: 2.0.0
URL: https://um-kevinhe.github.io/BregSurv/
Authors@R: c(
    person("Yubo","Shao",role=c("aut","cre"),email="ybshao@umich.edu")
  )
Description: Borrows external information when fitting a time-to-event model,
    through one objective: the target log-likelihood plus an integration weight times a Bregman
    divergence between the target and external models. The form in which the external source
    released its information fixes the divergence: individual-level records give a composite
    likelihood, coefficients with their uncertainty a Mahalanobis distance, and a fitted model or
    risk score alone a Kullback-Leibler divergence. The target may be a stratified Cox model, with
    tied event times or a nested case-control design, or a discrete-time model, with a linear or
    neural-network risk score and an optional ridge, lasso or elastic-net penalty. The integration
    weight is chosen by cross-validation on the target data.
